    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Developer Overview – FOI Fee Processing (router)\n\n**Purpose:**\nSingle entry point for every fee / payment event. It normalises the incoming event into a `feeAction` and hands it to the right sub-workflow. It holds no business logic itself.\n\n**Trigger/Entry:**\nSub-workflow. The `Start` node has fixed fields (the union of the fields below); a caller must map every field it has, anything it does not send stays empty. Callers: FOI Request Routing (foi-fee-payment, foi-manage-payment), FOI IAO Complete Process (initiate / cancel), FOI IAO Correspondence Process (initiate) and FOI Payment Expiry SLA Job (expire).\n\n**Routing (`Fee Action Router`):**\n- initiate → **FOI Fee Initiation** (create the online payment, SLA row, Form.io submission, applicant notification)\n- paid / cancel / expire → **FOI Fee Payment Outcome** (close the SLA row, update Form.io, confirmation / expiry email)\n- anything else → audit \"unsupported fee event\" and stop\n\n**Fields:**\nevent, eventId, occurredAt, feeAction, triggeredBy, category, paymentStatus, serviceKey, templateName, applicantCorrespondenceId, rawRequestId, foiRequestId, ministryRequestId, fileNumber, status, previousStatus, assignedTo, assignedGroup, isPaymentActive, isSync, isOfflinePayment, paymentExpiryDate, metadata, executionId, paymentSlaId, paymentUrl, slaPaymentExpiryDate, saveDataPayload, feeflow.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "a0e75407-a2df-462d-b29d-848d0a0fcea7",
      "name": "Developer Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        0
      ]
    }
